<h2>Local details that shape an Austin lighting design</h2>
<p>A few conditions come up on almost every Austin job. First, limestone. On the west side the soil is often only a few inches deep over caliche and rock, so wire runs are planned around what the ground allows and fixture stakes are chosen accordingly. Second, oak wilt. We never nail or screw fixtures into live oaks, and we avoid any pruning cuts to oaks during the spring transmission window; tree-mounted downlights are installed with adjustable straps that can be loosened as the tree grows. Third, heat. Austin summers push fixture housings and transformers hard, so we specify solid brass and copper bodies and size transformers with headroom.</p>
